<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_37" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_37">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_37" name="BPMN-37 | Product and Variant Maintenance" processRef="Process_37" />
    <bpmn:participant id="Cloudinary_37" name="Cloudinary — product image storage" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="UploadRequest_37" sourceRef="Upload_37" targetRef="Cloudinary_37" name="Validated image upload" />
    <bpmn:messageFlow id="UploadResponse_37" sourceRef="Cloudinary_37" targetRef="Upload_37" name="Stored media reference or failure" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_37" name="Product and Variant Maintenance" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-37, full catalog boundaries and shared-process rules; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.5 FR-CAT-01-05; supporting FR-PRICE-11-13, FR-BOM-07-08, NFR-SEC-03,08-09, NFR-REL-01-03,05-06, BR-24 and the documented Cloudinary image-storage integration. Implementation: index.html loads app/owner-products.js product/variant forms, confirmActivation and submit handler, app/pricing-state.js P.setPrice, app/staff-integration.js I.productAvailable, app/catalog.js and app/product.js. Current docs XMLs reviewed for convention/reuse, especially BPMN-27/30/35/36. SRS governs differences: preview image selection uses predefined assets; proposed upload validation/storage follows documented external-media support. No provider-specific transformation, file limit or upload endpoint is invented. Admin/Owner is the only editor; authentication is upstream BPMN-30, rechecked at protected saves. Local validation and exceptions are on the main diagram; external Cloudinary is a black-box pool with message flows, no generic broadcast signal. Scope is one catalog maintenance request covering create/update product or variant, activation/deactivation and subscription eligibility. Product name/description/image, applicable category association and per-variant label/active state are maintained without expanding independent category administration. Recipe/Bill of Materials and costing/final-price approval are separately owned by BPMN-39/40; supplied saved references/reviewed prices are used here, not automatically recalculated or approved. No BPMN-39/40 XML exists at authoring time, so references are visible rule/annotation references, not unresolved external call activities or fake embedded subprocesses. Product creation may save before a recipe is ready; no ready recipe means no ordering eligibility, not invented catalog-record rejection. Final prices must be valid owner-selected values where required for selected sellable variants; suggestions never replace them automatically. New subscription offerings/schedules belong to BPMN-38/03; this process records eligibility and does not enroll customers or alter paid subscription commitments. A combined product editor must validate dependent draft recipe/price/schedule changes under their owning rules and avoid partial saves. Availability reflects saved activation plus independent variant/recipe/stock constraints (BPMN-27 and checkout BPMN-09); activation alone does not promise stock or capacity. Failed writes retain existing catalog and transaction snapshots; media failure cannot publish a partially saved product. No deletion of historical products/variants, paid-order rewriting, price recomputation of purchased items, owner allocation, checkout, payment or marketing is introduced. Recoverable failures now remain in the same editing process with explicit review/edit/retry/stop paths. Recovery refreshes current data, guards stale drafts, reuses successful media and known successful operation results, and revalidates before protected writes. End events are reserved for success, denied access or administrator cancellation/stopping. No earlier BPMN is revised by this correction.</bpmn:documentation>
