    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_37" name="Administrator requests product or variant maintenance">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Access_37" name="Check administrator access; load catalog entry and current version">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-CAT-03-04; NFR-SEC-03. Require Admin/Owner before exposing maintenance controls. Load existing product/variant where selected, catalog/version context and saved recipe/price references; new product/variant has no existing target. Staff cannot edit catalog or owner pricing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Allowed_37" name="Administrator access and target valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_3</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="AccessError_37" name="Explain permission, missing target or load failure; retain catalog">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="AccessEnd_37" name="Maintenance blocked; no changes">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:userTask id="Edit_37" name="Create/edit product or variant; set images, availability and subscription eligibility">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-CAT-01-05. Edit product name/description/images, supported category association and variant labels/status; select activation/deactivation and subscription eligibility. Review existing variant final prices; if a price/recipe is changed, use BPMN-40/39 rules rather than catalog auto-pricing. Prototype separate variant form preserves existing prices on label/status edits. Deactivation prevents new selection, not fulfillment of paid orders. Unselecting a variant must not delete purchased references. Multiple variant support does not require a separate product for each variation.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_31</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Confirm_37" name="Administrator confirms requested changes?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_7</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="Cancel_37" name="Cancelled; saved catalog retained">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="Validate_37" name="Validate catalog fields, variant references and related saved inputs">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-CAT-01-05; NFR-SEC-08. Validate action/target/version, applicable product name/description/category/image choice and supported variants. Prototype requires name/description, valid category, at least one selected variant on product save, unique variant label within product and positive finite selected final prices. Apply only fields relevant to current operation; activation-only does not require re-entering product/price. Reuse saved recipe references (BPMN-39) and owner-reviewed final price inputs (BPMN-40); distinguish valid draft catalog creation from missing ordering readiness. Never infer zero/missing cost as a price or change approved final price from a suggestion. Subscription eligibility refers to future offerings; do not rewrite confirmed schedule/address/amount commitments. If dependent edits accompany same form, validate them under their owning rules before any combined save.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_34</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Valid_37" name="Catalog input and version valid?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_9</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_10</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_12</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="InputError_37" name="Explain input/version issue; retain editable draft and saved catalog">
      <bpmn:documentation>Return exact issue; correct relevant input or reopen latest entry. Preserve latest saved catalog, recipe/price and existing purchases. Do not invent unique product-name constraint or require complete stock just to save a catalog record.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_11</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="NewImage_37" name="Selected image still needs upload?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Upload only new/changed selected media without an already successful usable upload reference. An unchanged successfully stored image is reused after local save failure. A failed upload retains the proposed file for validation/retry; choosing a different file invalidates prior validation/reference.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_12</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_13</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_14</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:businessRuleTask id="CheckImage_37" name="Validate uploaded image type and size before storage">
      <bpmn:documentation>NFR-SEC-09. Permit only supported image file types/sizes under configured rules; reject unsupported/executable content. Do not invent a size limit or assume file extension alone is sufficient. Existing validated media selection/reference bypasses a new upload.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_13</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_15</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:businessRuleTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="ImageValid_37" name="Image permitted?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_15</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_16</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_18</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="ImageError_37" name="Explain unsupported image; retain draft for correction">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_16</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_17</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Upload_37" name="Store validated product image through Cloudinary">
      <bpmn:documentation>Use supported protected integration; return usable media reference or safe provider failure. Keep current catalog/image until final save succeeds. No unsupported automatic deletion of remote assets after a later local failure. Upload alone does not activate or publish product.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_18</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_19</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Uploaded_37" name="Usable image reference returned?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_19</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_20</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_22</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="UploadError_37" name="Explain upload failure; retain file and draft for safe retry">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_20</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_21</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Save_37" name="Save product/variant changes, activation and subscription eligibility consistently">
      <bpmn:documentation>Recheck administrator session/action permission, target and current catalog/dependent version at commit. Create distinct product/variant or update existing fields; retain stable references to inactive variants needed by history. Preserve unchanged saved recipe and final price; supplied combined recipe/price/schedule drafts must save consistently only after owning rule validation. Save activation/deactivation and subscription flag, supported media reference and catalog version together. Failed combined update commits no partial catalog/dependent changes; preserve independently committed newer state. Use safe repeated-operation identity/record context to avoid duplicate creates. Never rewrite purchased item price/quantity/configuration snapshots, subscription amounts/schedules or preparing-owner shares.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_22</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_14</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_23</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Saved_37" name="Catalog changes saved?">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_23</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_24</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_26</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="SaveError_37" name="Explain save/conflict failure; retain draft and successful media reference">
      <bpmn:documentation>No partial published product, activation flag, variant, price or recipe update. Refresh/review before retry; reuse known completed request result rather than duplicate creation. Existing remote upload does not mean catalog save succeeded. Old purchase commitments remain intact.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_24</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_25</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Refresh_37" name="Refresh storefront details and applicable ordering/subscription eligibility">
      <bpmn:documentation>FR-CAT-01-05. Show saved product information, images, variant/final price and availability consistently. Inactive product/variant cannot be selected for new transactions. Active still requires applicable recipe/stock controls owned by BPMN-27/shared inventory rules and final checkout BPMN-09; no ingredient/capacity reservation here. Subscription flag makes applicable configured offerings eligible for future enrollment through BPMN-03/38; it does not create a schedule or activate prepaid subscriptions. Preserve existing confirmed commitments when catalog eligibility is removed. A display refresh failure does not roll back a successfully saved catalog; refresh safely from saved records.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_37</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_26</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_37_27</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_37" name="Catalog maintained; storefront reflects saved availability">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_37_27</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_37_1" sourceRef="Start_37" targetRef="Access_37" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_37_2" sourceRef="Access_37" targetRef="Allowed_37" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_37_3" sourceRef="Allowed_37" targetRef="AccessError_37" name="No" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_37_4" sourceRef="AccessError_37" targetRef="AccessEnd_37" />
